<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (Women with disabilities face significant discrimination and stigma from their family members, society, and healthcare providers. They struggle to gain acceptance within their families and communities, and often encounter substantial challenges in accessing SRH-related information and healthcare services. These challenges stem from various barriers, such as physical and structural obstacles that hinder their ability to reach and utilize health facilities, and a lack of sensitivity and understanding from healthcare professionals.  )
/E (Women with disabilities face significant discrimination and stigma from their family members, society, and healthcare providers. They struggle to gain acceptance within their families and communities, and often encounter substantial challenges in accessing SRH-related information and healthcare services. These challenges stem from various barriers, such as physical and structural obstacles that hinder their ability to reach and utilize health facilities, and a lack of sensitivity and understanding from healthcare professionals.  )
/Alt ()
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
