/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (Possible, in partnership with WOREC, designed and piloted an intervention called MILAP, which stands for "unity and reconciliation" in Nepali. This family-based intervention is designed to help women experiencing intimate partner violence \(IPV\) by involving their husbands and mothers-in-law. In the first round of our pilot study conducted among young married women aged 15-24 years \(25 families\), MILAP proved to be safe, practical, and effective, leading to a significant reduction in depression among the women. )
/E (Possible, in partnership with WOREC, designed and piloted an intervention called MILAP, which stands for "unity and reconciliation" in Nepali. This family-based intervention is designed to help women experiencing intimate partner violence \(IPV\) by involving their husbands and mothers-in-law. In the first round of our pilot study conducted among young married women aged 15-24 years \(25 families\), MILAP proved to be safe, practical, and effective, leading to a significant reduction in depression among the women. )
